# Lines HttpDesk read as files before ADR 0010, which VS Code and Rider send as
# text: so does HttpDesk now, and the editor warns on each one. A File line is
# `<` or `<@` at the very start of a line, then a space or a tab, then the path.

@echo = https://httpbin.org/anything

### 1. No space after `<`: sent as the text "<../files/payload.json", with a warning
POST {{echo}}/no-space
Content-Type: application/json

<../files/payload.json

### 2. Indented: sent as text, with a warning
POST {{echo}}/indented
Content-Type: application/json

  < ../files/payload.json
